flags: --optimize whole

--- OUT --->
1482495
--- IR --->
// **the loop vectorises, and that is the assertion** - the same one `iteration/lowered_cost` makes and for
// the same reason it is spelled this way. a loop LoopVectorize widened is one it could prove has no calls,
// no aliasing hazard and a computable trip count, so `has_value()` and `unwrap()` are inlined away and the
// enum is SROA'd into registers, or none of this would be here.
//
// asking for the vector body **by name** is deliberate: the directives are plain substrings, so a bare
// `CHECK: body:` would match `vector.body:` and the test would silently stop describing the loop it names.
//
// what it pins about this type is the whole performance claim behind it being an enum: a `result<T, E>` over
// payloads that own nothing costs a tag test, and there is no call left to either contract
CHECK: define noundef i32 @main
CHECK: vector.body:
CHECK-NOT: call
CHECK-NOT: alloca
CHECK: br i1
